WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.690
In Iceland, on 14 April 2010, an eruption
begins at the summit of the volcano

2
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.910
Eyjafjallajökull.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.730
Scientists describe it as
an eruption of modest size.

4
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.370
It lasts 39 days.

5
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:18.070
Yet it causes unprecedented
disruption to air traffic.

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.530
It is the first Icelandic ash to reach
Europe since jet airliners came into use

7
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.510
in the 1960s.

8
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.670
So what turns a disaster
into a global one?

9
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.350
The size of the eruption?

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.750
The death toll?

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.510
In this mission, you'll
define a mega-disaster,

12
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:38.170
and trace the routes by which impacts
reach far beyond the place hit.

13
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.510
Then you'll compare developed,
emerging and developing countries,

14
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.850
weighing deaths against economic losses.

15
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.550
Your mission: explain what turns a
local disaster into a global one.
